  "description": "Sets up a local ADK Python development environment in a git clone of the open-source adk-python repository: a uv virtual environment, all dependency extras, pre-commit hooks, and a first unit-test run. Runs only when explicitly requested, never on its own. Use when asked to set up, bootstrap, or repair a development checkout, install project dependencies, fix a missing or broken .venv, or prepare a machine for contributing a pull request. Don't use for debugging a running agent (use adk-debug), for commit and pull-request mechanics (use adk-git), or for re-running formatters on a checkout that is already set up (pre-commit run --all-files).",
